# NimbusOS — Git attributes
#
# What: forces LF line endings for every text file in the repository.
# Why:  the repository is edited on Windows, but everything in it runs on
#       Debian. A CRLF in a shell script, debian/rules, a systemd unit or a
#       live-build hook breaks the build or the installed system. The
#       repository intentionally contains no binary files (images, fonts and
#       binary keyrings are generated at build time), so "text" is safe as the
#       default for everything.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Build products are never committed (see .gitignore), but if one is ever
# added by mistake, keep Git from rewriting its bytes.
*.iso  binary
*.deb  binary
*.gpg  binary
*.png  binary
*.pf2  binary
